.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Turning a camera picture upright, apart from the camera\&. 

A phone camera is fitted one way round and the phone is held another, so what the sensor reads is rarely what a person is looking at\&. SDL does not turn the picture for you; it measures how far it is out and hands that over with the frame, as SDL_PROP_SURFACE_ROTATION_FLOAT, leaving the turn to whoever is drawing\&.
.PP
The turn itself is arithmetic over a block of pixels, with no camera and no platform in it\&. It is declared here so that it can be tested against known pictures rather than against a device that has to be held a particular way round\&.
.PP
\fBNot part of the host facing interface\&.\fP A host binds to \fBschultz_api\&.h\fP\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_camera_internal\&.h\fP\&.
